From: FIRERED project
Subject: [PATCH 13] Decouple retail Pokédex storage from expanded species count

Applies after:
    patches/0007-gen10-save-schema.patch
    patches/0008-extended-dex-flags.patch

Reference target: pret/pokefirered
Reference snapshot: c75f352304d529f6ba92d4f74b9cf8b5c3810788

Retail FireRed derives DEX_FLAGS_NO from NUM_SPECIES. That is harmless while
NUM_SPECIES is 412, but it becomes a save-ABI bug as soon as later-generation
species are added: Pokedex.owned/seen and SaveBlock1 seen1/seen2 would grow,
moving every following save field.

Freeze the native storage at the exact retail footprint:
    DEX_FLAGS_NO = 0x34 = 52 bytes

Also separate the native National Dex boundary (Deoxys / 386) from the logical
NATIONAL_DEX_COUNT. The latter is expected to grow when later-generation
species are imported. Only IDs 1..386 may touch the retail anti-cheat arrays;
387..4096 use the extension bitsets introduced by patches 0007/0008.

--- a/include/global.h
+++ b/include/global.h
@@
 #define ROUND_BITS_TO_BYTES(numBits) DIV_ROUND_UP(numBits, 8)
 
-#define DEX_FLAGS_NO ROUND_BITS_TO_BYTES(NUM_SPECIES)
+#define FIRERED_RETAIL_DEX_FLAGS_NO 0x34
+#define FIRERED_RETAIL_NATIONAL_DEX_COUNT NATIONAL_DEX_DEOXYS
+#define DEX_FLAGS_NO FIRERED_RETAIL_DEX_FLAGS_NO
 #define NUM_FLAG_BYTES ROUND_BITS_TO_BYTES(FLAGS_COUNT)
 #define NUM_ADDITIONAL_PHRASE_BYTES ROUND_BITS_TO_BYTES(NUM_ADDITIONAL_PHRASES)

--- a/src/pokedex_screen.c
+++ b/src/pokedex_screen.c
@@
-    if (nationalDexNo > NATIONAL_DEX_COUNT)
+    if (nationalDexNo > FIRERED_RETAIL_NATIONAL_DEX_COUNT)
         return FireredExtendedDexGetSetFlag(nationalDexNo, caseId);
